menu "Moon Phase Asset Configuration"

    config MOON_ALBEDO_W
        int "Equirect albedo texture width (px; height = width / 2)"
        # Kconfig evaluates multiple default lines FIRST-MATCH-WINS, so the
        # conditional line must precede the unconditional fallback.
        default 2048 if BOARD_P4
        default 864
        range 864 4096
        help
            The width of the equirect 2:1 albedo texture (in pixels; the
            height is width/2) baked from the 4096x2048 16-bit LROC
            source by the asset pipeline (assets/images/moon, gitignored)
            and flashed into the moon_assets partition. Both boards
            default to the best resolution their flash + PSRAM budgets
            allow (resolution over speed):

              S3 (16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM): 864 (432) -- 2,470,400 B of
                  the 2560K partition; 864 is the max the PSRAM pool can
                  spare (1024 would fill the partition exactly but adds
                  ~0.45 MB of asset PSRAM the pool cannot spare).
              P4 (32 MB flash, 32 MB PSRAM): 2048 (1024) -- 4,194,304 B
                  of the 5120K partition; matches the 2048-wide relief
                  DEM grid (1.57x oversampling at the 650 px disk).

            The width must be EVEN (equirect 2:1) and must match the
            generated assets: the root CMakeLists FATAL_ERRORs on an
            odd width or on a moon_assets.bin whose manifest width
            differs from this value, and refuses a blob that overflows
            the board's moon_assets partition (naming the KiB it needs).
            After changing it, regenerate the affected target:
              cd assets/images/moon && .venv/bin/python -m moon.assets \
                  --target p4 --alb 2560x1280
            (the Kconfig value only selects which pre-baked texture the
            build flashes; the texture itself is produced by the
            pipeline, never at compile time).

endmenu
